      "description": "Biometric Information Privacy Act",
      "weight": 100,
      "data": {
        "official_name": "Biometric Information Privacy Act",
        "common_name": "BIPA",
        "alternate_names": [
          "740 ILCS 14"
        ],
        "description": "Illinois law regulating the collection, use, storage, and destruction of biometric identifiers and information.",
        "notes": "Effective 2008. The most significant US biometric privacy law due to its private right of action. Requires informed written consent before collection of biometric identifiers (fingerprints, retina/iris scans, voiceprints, hand/face geometry). Mandates retention schedule and destruction guidelines. Prohibits sale or profit from biometric data. Private right of action with statutory damages: $1,000 per negligent violation, $5,000 per intentional/reckless violation. Has generated extensive litigation, particularly against tech companies and employers using biometric time clocks.",
        "urls": [
          {
            "type": "website",
